# Presentation follows DESIGN.md

When editing UI, **read [DESIGN.md](../../DESIGN.md)** first. It is the visual contract. Do not invent a second design system.

## Obligations

- Map colors, type, and radius to DESIGN.md tokens (Flame Red `#e11d48` as the **only** interactive accent).
- Use shadcn/ui + Tailwind as specified in DESIGN.md section 3.
- Reuse named patterns: Metric Tile, Raw Material Waste Input Row, Live Order Queue Item — do not restyle them ad hoc.
- Font weights: 300 / 400 / 600 / 700 only — **never** weight 500.
- Surfaces: flat cards, 1px hairline borders — **no** `shadow-lg` / `shadow-2xl`.
- Numbers always show units or thresholds (`kg`, `g`, `%`).

## Scaffold

The `with-supabase` starter may not match DESIGN.md. **DESIGN.md wins for new UI.** Do not restyle the whole scaffold unless a spec requires it.

## Layers

Pages are view containers (`docs/architecture.md`). Domain and application stay free of visual tokens. Details: `docs/conventions.md` Presentation / UI.
